before:
A reference declares which key must exist.
```sql
CREATE TABLE teams (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY);
CREATE TABLE players (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  team_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES teams(id)
);
```

The parent row must exist before its child is inserted.
```sql
INSERT INTO teams VALUES (8);
INSERT INTO players VALUES (1, 8);
```

after:
Run this example in a fresh database:
```sql
PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
CREATE TABLE teams(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY);
CREATE TABLE players (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  team_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES teams(id)
);
INSERT INTO teams VALUES (8);
INSERT INTO players VALUES (1, 8);
SELECT id, team_id
FROM players;
```
Player `1` belongs to team `8`.
